  "notes": "A Philly soul production duo out of DJ Jazzy Jeff's A Touch of Jazz, 1996–2010. **The research states a deliberate boundary and it is honoured here: their Musiq Soulchild and Jill Scott work belongs to the neo-soul lane, and this entry covers only their radio-R&B placements.** The band is \"70–100 straight\", marked `[LOW-CONF]`, used as written with the mode at 88. Three drum deltas from the lineage claim: \"A Touch of Jazz lineage means a live-feel, lightly swung kit over a programmed base — backbeat on 2&4, played hat/ride, hand percussion\", also `[LOW-CONF]`. So the hat is a played 8th base at 0.34 fill density rather than a gridded 16th, the snare carries ghosts on three off-slots 4–9 ms late, and the perc bed is a four-lane ride/conga/shaker/rim set at three to six hits a bar, with `quantizeStrength` at 0.6 and `velocityVar` 0.26. The research's own summary of them is structural rather than sonic — they work as \"**producers-plus-engineers** (producing, songwriting, mixing and recording engineering in one team)\" and \"came together as solo hip-hop artists before moving into production, so **the rhythm grid stays hip-hop even under soul harmony**\". That last sentence is the model: a swung, hip-hop-weighted kit under Philly-soul changes — \"extended major and minor chords with real cadences\", so the triad share falls to 0.12 and ninth to 0.38 over four-chord functional families. The bass is \"played bass with walking motion rather than sustained 808\", so `followRootsProb` 0.48 with walking cells and no `bass808` block. ⚠ Confidence is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low and marks the drum, harmony and bass claims `[LOW-CONF]` — \"the parametric detail is Philly-soul-lane inference\". ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"Philly-soul harmonic language — extended major and minor chords with real cadences [LOW-CONF]\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
